# Allowed govulncheck findings in the child binaries hack/release/stage.sh stages.
#
# stage.sh scans every staged Go child (govulncheck -mode=binary) after staging
# and before signing, and reds on any finding whose trace reaches a vulnerable
# symbol in the binary unless a line below names it. One entry per line:
#
#   <GO-id> <child> <child-version> <reason> <expiry YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# <child> is the staged name (helm without its version suffix) and
# <child-version> the pin it was built or downloaded at, so a pin bump makes the
# entry match nothing and the finding is reviewed again. The reason is required
# (at least 20 characters) and says why shipping the finding is acceptable until
# the expiry, which is at most 120 days out. An expired entry is a red. An entry
# that matches no symbol-level finding in a scan is a red too: delete it, so
# exemptions do not outlive what they excused.
#
# GO-2026-5932 marks golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp deprecated and names no
# vulnerable symbols, so govulncheck lists every openpgp package ("/*") for any
# binary that links golang.org/x/crypto, whatever packages of it the binary
# uses. kubectl links no x/crypto and reports clean. helm v4.3.1 links x/crypto
# v0.58.0 and the three kube daemons below v0.57.0, for other packages; none of them
# names an x/crypto/openpgp package path, and helm's OpenPGP code (chart
# provenance) is github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto. The v1.37.1 source vendors
# no x/crypto/openpgp package.
GO-2026-5932 helm v4.3.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.58.0 GO-2026-5932 names no symbols, so govulncheck reports every openpgp package of any binary that links golang.org/x/crypto at all; this binary names no x/crypto/openpgp package path, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
GO-2026-5932 kube-apiserver v1.37.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 GO-2026-5932 names no symbols, so govulncheck reports every openpgp package of any binary that links golang.org/x/crypto at all; this binary names no x/crypto/openpgp package path, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
GO-2026-5932 kube-scheduler v1.37.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 GO-2026-5932 names no symbols, so govulncheck reports every openpgp package of any binary that links golang.org/x/crypto at all; this binary names no x/crypto/openpgp package path, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
GO-2026-5932 kube-controller-manager v1.37.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 GO-2026-5932 names no symbols, so govulncheck reports every openpgp package of any binary that links golang.org/x/crypto at all; this binary names no x/crypto/openpgp package path, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
